From: rnsbox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] buildroot: SLIP default 2000000 on the LicheeRV Nano

With the uart reclock the board generates the modem's factory 2 Mbaud
exactly, so the shipped slip.conf/S31slip defaults stop papering over
the old 25 MHz/16 = 1,562,500 ceiling with 1500000 (which only fitted
the line to +4.17% anyway). Fallback advice becomes 1000000 — also
exact at 96 MHz (quot 6) — replacing 921600, which is -7% there.

This is the capability delta for the rv64 LicheeRV Nano; the arm64
board gets the same default from the shared series and its own dts
reclock in milkv-duo-01-arm.
diff --git a/README.RNSBox.md b/README.RNSBox.md
index cae0844..fa53ce3 100644
--- a/README.RNSBox.md
+++ b/README.RNSBox.md
@@ -133,21 +133,23 @@ versa:
 | `GPIOA29`  | UART1_RX | TX            |
 | `GND`      | ground   | GND           |
 
-Keep the leads short — at 1.5 Mbaud, long unshielded jumpers invite frame errors.
+Keep the leads short — at 2 Mbaud, long unshielded jumpers invite frame errors.
 
 ### Baud
 
-Both ends must run the **same baud**. The Nano-e's UART is clocked from 25 MHz,
-so its ceiling is **1,562,500** (25 MHz / 16) — it cannot reach the modem's
-2,000,000 default. Use **1500000** on both sides:
+Both ends must run the **same baud**. The LicheeRV Nano dts reclocks
+`clk_cam0_200` to disppll/8 = 96 MHz before the 8250 probes, so the modem's
+factory **2000000** is generated exactly (96 MHz / 16 / 3) — keep it on both
+sides:
 
-- **Modem**: set SLIP baud to `1500000` over its Ethernet web UI (or `POST
-  /api/slip_cfg`). Runtime-settable and persisted — no reflash.
-- **RNSBox**: `baud=1500000` in the *HaLow modem (SLIP)* card (or
-  `/etc/rnsbox/slip.conf`).
+- **Modem**: leave the factory SLIP baud `2000000` (verify in its Ethernet
+  web UI, or `POST /api/slip_cfg`). Runtime-settable and persisted — no
+  reflash.
+- **RNSBox**: `baud=2000000` in the *HaLow modem (SLIP)* card (or
+  `/etc/rnsbox/slip.conf` — the shipped default here).
 
 If `rx_over_errors` climbs under load (`ip -s link show sl0`), drop both ends to
-`1000000` or `921600`.
+`1000000` (also exact on this 96 MHz clock: 96 MHz / 16 / 6).
 
 ### Bring it up
 
diff --git a/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S31slip b/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S31slip
index 6f220d5..8e292b8 100644
--- a/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S31slip
+++ b/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/init.d/S31slip
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ start() {
 	case "$enabled" in yes|true|1|on) ;; *) echo "S31slip: disabled"; return 0 ;; esac
 
 	device=$(cfg device);     [ -n "$device" ]   || device=/dev/ttyS1
-	baud=$(cfg baud);         [ -n "$baud" ]     || baud=1500000
+	baud=$(cfg baud);         [ -n "$baud" ]     || baud=2000000
 	local_ip=$(cfg local_ip); [ -n "$local_ip" ] || local_ip=192.168.7.1
 	peer_ip=$(cfg peer_ip);   [ -n "$peer_ip" ]  || peer_ip=192.168.7.2
 
diff --git a/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/rnsbox/slip.conf b/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/rnsbox/slip.conf
index 207320d..8b3177f 100644
--- a/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/rnsbox/slip.conf
+++ b/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/rnsbox/slip.conf
@@ -13,14 +13,16 @@
 # Wiring (LicheeRV Nano-e): UART1 on GPIOA28 (TX) / GPIOA29 (RX), 3.3 V,
 # common ground — device = /dev/ttyS1. Do NOT use ttyS0 (console).
 #
-# baud MUST match the modem's SLIP baud. The Nano's UART tops out at
-# 1,562,500 (25 MHz/16); the modem defaults to 2,000,000 which the Nano
-# cannot reach, so set the modem to 1500000 (via its web UI) and match it
-# here. local_ip/peer_ip must match the modem's SLIP config (defaults
-# 192.168.7.2 device / 192.168.7.1 host).
+# baud MUST match the modem's SLIP baud. The dts reclocks clk_cam0_200
+# to disppll/8 = 96 MHz before the 8250 probes, so the modem's factory
+# 2000000 is generated exactly (96M/16/3). Fallback with headroom for
+# frame errors: 1000000 (also exact, 96M/16/6). At the old fixed 25 MHz
+# uart clock the 8250 ceiling was 1,562,500, which is what 1500000 was
+# papering over. local_ip/peer_ip must match the modem's SLIP config
+# (defaults 192.168.7.2 device / 192.168.7.1 host).
 
 enabled=no
 device=/dev/ttyS1
-baud=1500000
+baud=2000000
 local_ip=192.168.7.1
 peer_ip=192.168.7.2
-- 
